state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e535f6ba926f8cc6f897f395c8c0cd2f63527b7455ee53447544fc3dce8ea8d</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--0152f72654ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecd7c42aad8118ebfe2ec59b00718dfcad642af608cdcd86a54fa342fbae7fa4</id><updated>2026-10-16T04:44:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
